{"entities":"[{\"text\": \"cardiotoxicity\", \"id\": \"D066126\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"nephrotoxicity\", \"id\": \"D007674\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"doxorubicin\", \"id\": \"D004317\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"immunocytoma\", \"id\": \"-1\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"cardiotoxicity\", \"id\": \"D066126\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"nephrotoxicity\", \"id\": \"D007674\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"doxorubicin\", \"id\": \"D004317\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"immunocytoma\", \"id\": \"-1\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"tumor\", \"id\": \"D009369\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"doxorubicin\", \"id\": \"D004317\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"Tumor\", \"id\": \"D009369\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"doxorubicin\", \"id\": \"D004317\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"tumor\", \"id\": \"D009369\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"doxorubicin\", \"id\": \"D004317\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"cardiotoxicity\", \"id\": \"D066126\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"doxorubicin\", \"id\": \"D004317\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"renal damage\", \"id\": \"D007674\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"doxorubicin\", \"id\": \"D004317\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"albuminuria\", \"id\": \"D000419\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"doxorubicin\", \"id\": \"D004317\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"Ascites\", \"id\": \"D001201\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"hydrothorax\", \"id\": \"D006876\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"tumor\", \"id\": \"D009369\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"cardiotoxicity\", \"id\": \"D066126\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"nephrotoxicity\", \"id\": \"D007674\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"Albuminuria\", \"id\": \"D000419\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"renal damage\", \"id\": \"D007674\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"ascites\", \"id\": \"D001201\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"hydrothorax\", \"id\": \"D006876\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"cardiomyopathy\", \"id\": \"D009202\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}]","filtered_entities":[{"text":"cardiotoxicity","id":"D066126","label":"Disease"},{"text":"nephrotoxicity","id":"D007674","label":"Disease"},{"text":"doxorubicin","id":"D004317","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"immunocytoma","id":"-1","label":"Disease"},{"text":"tumor","id":"D009369","label":"Disease"},{"text":"renal damage","id":"D007674","label":"Disease"},{"text":"albuminuria","id":"D000419","label":"Disease"},{"text":"Ascites","id":"D001201","label":"Disease"},{"text":"hydrothorax","id":"D006876","label":"Disease"},{"text":"cardiomyopathy","id":"D009202","label":"Disease"}],"head":"doxorubicin","head_id":"D004317","pairs":[{"head":"doxorubicin","tail":"cardiotoxicity","head_id":"D004317","tail_id":"D066126"},{"head":"doxorubicin","tail":"nephrotoxicity","head_id":"D004317","tail_id":"D007674"},{"head":"doxorubicin","tail":"immunocytoma","head_id":"D004317","tail_id":"-1"},{"head":"doxorubicin","tail":"tumor","head_id":"D004317","tail_id":"D009369"},{"head":"doxorubicin","tail":"albuminuria","head_id":"D004317","tail_id":"D000419"},{"head":"doxorubicin","tail":"Ascites","head_id":"D004317","tail_id":"D001201"},{"head":"doxorubicin","tail":"hydrothorax","head_id":"D004317","tail_id":"D006876"},{"head":"doxorubicin","tail":"cardiomyopathy","head_id":"D004317","tail_id":"D009202"}],"relations":["D004317 | D066126","D004317 | D007674","D004317 | D000419","D004317 | D001201","D004317 | D006876","D004317 | D009202"],"result":"$","tail":"cardiomyopathy","tail_id":"D009202","text":"Antitumor effect, cardiotoxicity, and nephrotoxicity of doxorubicin in the IgM solid immunocytoma-bearing LOU/M/WSL rat. Antitumor activity, cardiotoxicity, and nephrotoxicity induced by doxorubicin were studied in LOU/M/WSL inbred rats each bearing a transplantable solid IgM immunocytoma. Animals with a tumor (diameter, 15.8 +/- 3.3 mm) were treated with iv injections of doxorubicin on 5 consecutive days, followed by 1 weekly injection for 7 weeks (dose range, 0.015-4.0 mg/kg body wt). Tumor regression was observed with 0.5 mg doxorubicin/kg. Complete disappearance of the tumor was induced with 1.0 mg doxorubicin/kg. Histologic evidence of cardiotoxicity scored as grade III was only observed at a dose of 1.0 mg doxorubicin/kg. Light microscopic evidence of renal damage was seen above a dose of 0.5 mg doxorubicin/kg, which resulted in albuminuria and very low serum albumin levels. In the group that received 1.0 mg doxorubicin/kg, the serum albumin level decreased from 33.6 +/- 4.1 to 1.5 +/- 0.5 g/liter. Ascites and hydrothorax were observed simultaneously. The same experiments were performed with non-tumor-bearing rats, in which no major differences were observed. In conclusion, antitumor activity, cardiotoxicity, and nephrotoxicity were studied simultaneously in the same LOU/M/WSL rat. Albuminuria due to renal damage led to extremely low serum albumin levels, so ascites and hydrothorax were not necessarily a consequence of the observed cardiomyopathy.","metrics":{"precision":0.5,"recall":1.0,"f1":0.6666666666666666,"rel_tp":3,"rel_fp":3,"rel_fn":0}}